window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-cad447b4f59d31e1"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"track-course-engagement\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">跟踪课程参与情况</h1> <p>将去标识化的课程导出数据整理成供教师审核的视图。</p> <p>使用 ChatGPT，根据 LMS 活动、成绩册、出勤、作业元数据和指标定义，制作一个仪表板，呈现参与模式、完成情况缺口、评估趋势和数据质量警告。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>需要审核课程参与情况和完成模式的教师。</li> <li>需要统一口径并检查数据质量的课程导出数据。</li> <li>需要支持人工审核、但不用于诊断学生的仪表板。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>$spreadsheets</code></td> <td>对齐课程导出数据、计算经审核的指标并制作可编辑仪表板。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>google-drive</code></td> <td>收集已批准的 LMS、出勤、成绩册和作业文件。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>制作课程参与度仪表板</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">请根据我提供的去标识化 LMS 活动、成绩册、出勤、作业元数据、课程日历和指标定义，制作课程参与情况与学习表现仪表板。\n\n请呈现：\n- 参与趋势\n- 完成情况缺口\n- 评估模式\n- 缺失或不一致的数据\n- 供教师审核的问题\n\n请创建教师审核队列。不要诊断学生，也不要自动执行联系、评分、分班或支持决策。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"define-the-dashboard-before-combining-data\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">合并数据前先定义仪表板</h2> <p>只提供已批准且经过去标识化处理的导出数据。附上指标定义、报告时间范围、课程日历，以及用于对齐文件所需的标识信息。</p> <p>在制作图表前，请 ChatGPT 说明将如何关联 LMS、出勤、成绩册和作业数据。先解决重复记录、缺失标识和定义冲突。</p> <p><a id=\"build-a-review-view\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">制作审核视图</h2> <p>使用起始提示词创建仪表板，其中包括：</p> <ul> <li>随时间变化的趋势</li> <li>作业完成情况和评估模式</li> <li>与课程结构相符的筛选器</li> <li>缺失数据和数据质量警告</li> <li>供教师审核的问题队列</li> </ul> <p>将观察到的模式与对模式的解释分开。活动发生变化只是值得检查的信号，并不代表已经找到了原因。</p> <p><a id=\"validate-and-use-responsibly\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">验证并负责任地使用</h2> <p>对照源数据总量检查计算结果，并抽查单条去标识化记录。确认日期范围、教学班筛选器和评估分组均正确。</p> <p>使用仪表板来引导教师提出问题。不要用它自动评分、联系学生、分班或生成高风险标签。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"track-course-engagement\">Track course engagement</h1> <p>Turn de-identified course exports into a faculty review view.</p> <p>Use ChatGPT with LMS activity, gradebook, attendance, assignment metadata, and metric definitions to build a dashboard of engagement patterns, completion gaps, assessment trends, and data-quality warnings.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Faculty reviewing course engagement and completion patterns.</li> <li>Course exports that need aligned definitions and data-quality checks.</li> <li>Dashboards that support human review without diagnosing students.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>$spreadsheets</code></td> <td>Align course exports, calculate reviewed metrics, and build an editable dashboard.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>google-drive</code></td> <td>Gather approved LMS, attendance, gradebook, and assignment files.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Build a Course Engagement Dashboard</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Build a course engagement and performance dashboard from the de-identified LMS activity, gradebook, attendance, assignment metadata, course calendar, and metric definitions I provide.\n\nShow:\n- engagement trends\n- completion gaps\n- assessment patterns\n- missing or inconsistent data\n- questions for faculty review\n\nCreate a faculty review queue. Do not diagnose students or automate outreach, grading, placement, or support decisions.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugins</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"define-the-dashboard-before-combining-data\">Define the dashboard before combining data</h2> <p>Provide only approved, de-identified exports. Include the metric definitions, reporting window, course calendar, and identifiers needed to align the files.</p> <p>Before building charts, ask ChatGPT to show how the LMS, attendance, gradebook, and assignment data will be joined. Resolve duplicate records, missing identifiers, and conflicting definitions first.</p> <h2 id=\"build-a-review-view\">Build a review view</h2> <p>Use the starter prompt to create a dashboard with:</p> <ul> <li>trends over time</li> <li>assignment completion and assessment patterns</li> <li>filters that match the course structure</li> <li>missing-data and quality warnings</li> <li>a queue of questions for faculty review</li> </ul> <p>Keep observed patterns separate from explanations. A change in activity is a signal to inspect, not a diagnosis.</p> <h2 id=\"validate-and-use-responsibly\">Validate and use responsibly</h2> <p>Check calculations against source totals and spot-check individual de-identified records. Confirm that date windows, section filters, and assessment groupings are correct.</p> <p>Use the dashboard to guide faculty questions. Do not use it to automate grading, outreach, placement, or high-stakes labels.</p>"};
